    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` as the spec describes, keeping the signature and editing no other file. It validates the region, categories, quantities, prices, discounts and credit, and raises `ValueError` on bad input. Each line's net is its price times quantity, reduced by the line discount, then by the 5% bulk discount for standard lines of 10 or more, and rounded half-up to cents. Tax is computed per line on that rounded net and rounded the same way. Totals are summed from the rounded line values, and credit is applied against gross. `tax_by_rate` is keyed by integer rate and includes 0% lines. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was not available.",
